Replace-From: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
Replace-Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 00:17:21 +0800
Subject: [LOCAL] media: histb-vpss: failure dump for the bench


Kept out of the submitted series on purpose.
A failed vpss_v4_0 job prints the chain head, the latch and statistics words and the in-window block's own debug words; the readings they carried have all been replaced, so the dump is bring-up instrumentation and not evidence.
The register definitions only this dump consumes stay here too.
 3 files changed, 93 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)


diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/hisilicon,hi3798mv100-vpss.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/hisilicon,hi3798mv100-vpss.yaml
index c45ca6e1e7a9..d134a2d54e72 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/hisilicon,hi3798mv100-vpss.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/hisilicon,hi3798mv100-vpss.yaml
@@ -11,8 +11,8 @@ maintainers:
 
 description: |-
   The video processing subsystem sits between a decoder and an encoder or a
-  display: it converts a frame between YUV layouts, scales it, rotates it
-  and de-interlaces it. The block has its own register window, clock gate and
+  display: it linearises the decoder's 16x16-tiled frames, scales them and
+  de-interlaces them. The block has its own register window, clock gate and
   reset request in the clock and reset generator.
 
   Hi3798MV200 has the same block a generation on (its VPSS_VERSION answers
